      ],
      "expectation": "DATA-A01 All business requests go to base URL `https://mall.dusksnow.top/app/` (same for the dev and prod flavors) plus a relative path, sent as JSON with unknown response fields ignored\nDATA-A02 Main API client connect/read/write timeouts are 10 seconds each, and it retries on connection failure\nDATA-A03 When a token is stored locally, every business request carries header `Authorization` set to the raw token value (no `Bearer` prefix). Without a token the header is omitted\nDATA-A04 Every API response is parsed as an envelope { data, code, message }, and only `code == 1000` counts as success\nDATA-A05 On a business failure (code != 1000), the caller gets the server message (fallback `未知错误`), and with showToast on an error toast appears. Exceptions/network errors fall back to `网络请求失败`. There is no 401/token-expiry interception: no auto logout or redirect to login\nDATA-A06 Paged requests default to page=1, size=10, sort=`desc`. Responses are { list, pagination{ total, size, page } }, and there is a next page if `size*page < total`\nDATA-A19 Image upload works in two steps: first `base/comm/upload` returns temporary credentials and a url, then a multipart POST to that url (fields key=`app/base/{uuid}_image.{ext}`, tmpSecretId, tmpSecretKey, sessionToken, file). On success the image address is url + \"/\" + key\nDATA-A20 Batch image upload goes one by one; if any image fails, the whole batch fails with an error message prefixed `批量上传失败`. The upload client uses 30-second timeouts and sends no Authorization header\nAUTH-A32 After login, every request carries the stored token in the Authorization header (raw token, no Bearer prefix)",
