      "expectation": "LAUNCH-A19 At startup, login state is restored from the local `auth_info` record: it counts as logged in only when the token is non-empty and not expired (createdAt + expire seconds); only when logged in is user info read from local `user_info` and userId set\nLAUNCH-A21 On logout, local `auth_info` and `user_info` are cleared and the in-memory login state is reset to not logged in (userId=0)\nLAUNCH-A22 Global route login wall: when not logged in, navigating to profile/address list/address detail/order list/confirm order/order detail/payment/refund/review/logistics/support chat/coupons/feedback list/submit feedback is redirected to the login page (AuthRoutes.Login)\nDATA-A07 Login credentials are stored as JSON (token/refreshToken/expire/refreshExpire/createdAt) under persistence key `auth_info`\nDATA-A08 Logged in = local auth exists, token is non-empty and not expired (createdAt + expire seconds). An expired token counts as not logged in\nDATA-A09 User info (User) is stored as JSON under persistence key `user_info`, and it is read only when logged in\nDATA-A10 On cold start the app restores login state and user info from local storage: after login, a restarted app is still logged in and the user's nickname/avatar show without logging in again\nDATA-A11 After a successful login, auth and user are written to local storage and memory together, login state becomes true, and then the person-info endpoint is called to refresh user info\nDATA-A12 Logging out removes only `auth_info` and `user_info` and resets in-memory login state/userId=0. It calls no server endpoint and does not clear the local cart, footprints, search history or remembered account\nDATA-A13 Opening a login-required page (Profile, address list/detail, order list/confirm/detail/pay/refund/comment/logistics, customer-service chat, coupons, feedback list/submit) while not logged in sends the user to the login page instead",
