      "expectation": "MAIN-A01 Top content of the Category, Cart and Me tabs avoids the status bar (Scaffold content insets, navigation bar excluded only)\nMAIN-A02 The Category tab shows a centered title bar `分类` with no back button\nMAIN-A03 Opening the Category tab requests the category list once (POST goods/type/list) and builds a tree sorted by sortNum: items with null parentId are first-level categories, the rest attach under their parent by parentId\nMAIN-A04 While category data loads, the page shows the category skeleton (left/right two-column placeholders); loading lasts at least 320ms\nMAIN-A05 When category loading fails, the page shows the network error state `网络连接失败`/`请检查网络连接后重试` with a `重新加载` button; tapping it requests again\nMAIN-A06 After loading, the left column lists all first-level category names, with the first selected by default; the selected item is highlighted with a left indicator bar and cannot be tapped again\nMAIN-A07 The right column is one continuously scrolling list: each first-level category shows a lined title (category name) followed by a 3-column grid of its second-level categories (image + name); a category with no children shows only the title\nMAIN-A08 Tapping a first-level category on the left scrolls the right list to that category's section\nMAIN-A09 When the user scrolls the right list by hand, the left selection follows the category section currently in view (the two are linked, with no feedback loop)\nMAIN-A10 Tapping a second-level category goes to the goods category/list page (GoodsRoutes.Category) with that subcategory id as typeId",
